t_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"And we hadn't talked yet about what we believe the cost savings will be that come out of that transaction.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2018-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2018 Q3","e":"hwc","d":"2018-10-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"David Feaster","x":"Could you talk about maybe a run rate for trust fees in the fourth quarter and into next year and maybe whether there's any more specifics or updates with regard to the conversion in the first half of '19 and quantification of cost saving potential?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2018-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2018 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2019-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"Non-operating expense items for the quarter totaled $2.5 million and were partially offset by a $600,000 net gain on the sale of securities related to a portfolio restructuring we executed in the fourth quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2018-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2018 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2019-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"The VISA-B trade and related restructuring improves the Company's yields on investment securities and loans, while also improving our funding mix in 2019.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2018-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2019 Q1","e":"hwc","d":"2019-04-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John M. Hairston","x":"While a portion of the increase was related to the restructuring last quarter, we also saw a core improvement in yields and remain focused on adding more granular credits at a higher yield to continue narrowing the NIM gap to peers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q1-2019-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2019 Q1","e":"hwc","d":"2019-04-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"The margin expansion was mostly related to the full quarter impact of the portfolio restructuring we executed late in the fourth quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q1-2019-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2019 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2019-07-17","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"So while it's hard to predict the timing on this kind of income, we did increase our 2019 guidance slightly to reflect this.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/17/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q2-2019-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2019 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2020-01-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John M. Hairston","x":"I think we, again as I mentioned have opportunities to maybe outperform our loan growth guidance a bit, but we also have opportunities to potentially look at doing some restructuring our bond portfolio.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/16/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2019-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2019 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2020-01-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Jennifer Demba","x":"And, Mike, you mentioned earlier in the call, you are considering restructuring the balance sheet.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/16/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2019-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2020 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2020-07-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John M. Hairston","x":"And so I think over the course of the next quarter, as the deferrals are completely retired, as we know what the credits are that end up needing modest modifications versus additional restructuring, then we're going to see migrations based on actual risk ratings and not just sectors under focus.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/22/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q2-2020-earnings-c.aspx"},{"c":"HWC 2020 Q3","e":"hwc","d":"2020-10-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"So the severance that we had, as well as some of the costs related to the closure of some of the facilities we called out was really offset by the reduction in incentive comp and a few other items that were really, kind of, left over from the MSL acquisition.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2020-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2020 Q3","e":"hwc","d":"2020-10-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"Now in the fourth quarter we do expect to continue to execute on the same kinds of our cost initiatives -- cost-saving initiatives that we did in the third quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2020-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2020 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2021-01-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"And has recently as yesterday, we have continued implementing cost saving measures by offering an early retirement package to select employees across the Company.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2020-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2020 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2021-01-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Kevin Fitzsimmon","x":"So, when I look at Page 8, you discuss layoff people holding an effect on the margin.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2020-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q1","e":"hwc","d":"2021-04-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Brad Milsaps","x":"If you had to use that same analogy now, with the guidance that you've given, inclusive of 2022, where would you -- where would you sort of put Hancock Whitney in sort of your expense rightsizing journey?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/21/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q1-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2021-07-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John M. Hairston","x":"I do want to recognize and thank our entire team of associates for outperforming in nearly every category, while simultaneously working toward rightsizing our expense base.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q2-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2021-07-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John M. Hairston","x":"During the second quarter, we completed our previously announced phased in plan to streamline and strengthen our operational framework according to our clients' changing needs and habits in the recovering economy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q2-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q3","e":"hwc","d":"2021-10-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"As we move into the fourth quarter, we have maintained our guidance for core loan growth of $400 million to $500 million and PPP forgiveness of up to $500 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/19/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q3","e":"hwc","d":"2021-10-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Michael M. Achary","x":"We are maintaining our guidance for a fourth quarter expense level of $187 million and are committed to that run rate for 2022.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/19/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q3-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2021 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2022-01-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Michael Rose","x":"So can you just break down where the incremental cost savings are coming?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/01/19/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q4-2021-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2022 Q1","e":"hwc","d":"2022-04-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Mike Achary","x":"We expect fees will be a challenge moving forward and have lowered our guidance for 2022 to reflect both a rising rate environment and our announcement last month regarding the elimination of NSF and certain overdraft fees later this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/04/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q1-2022-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2022 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2022-07-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Hairston","x":"As the price increases get worked into our modeling, especially the 75 bps increase that happened in June, and we were modeling another 75 for July.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/07/20/hancock-whitney-corporation-hwc-q2-2022-earnings-c/"},{"c":"HWC 2025 Q2","e":"hwc","d":"2025-07-15","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Michael Rose","x":"It does seem know, if you listen to some of the larger guys today that I think we're at a point where even though there's still some uncertainty around tariffs and things like that, I think there's just a comfort level and borrowers are starting to move off the sidelines a little bit.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/07/15/hancock-whitney-hwc-q2-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"HWC 2025 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2026-01-20","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Shane Loper","x":"Mortgage fees, again, continue to perform and we're ready for anything that may happen in the mortgage market with direct to consumer digital offering that we have there.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/20/hancock-whitney-hwc-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"HWC 2025 Q4","e":"hwc","d":"2026-01-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Hairston","x":"On an annual basis, we expect the restructuring exercise to benefit NIM by seven basis points and EPS will improve $0.23 per share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/20/hancock-whitn